  "title": {
    "it": "Grammatica · 〜と思う / 〜と言う",
    "en": "Grammar · ~to omou / ~to iu"
  },
  "description": {
    "it": "Per esprimere opinioni e citare: 〜と思う ('penso che...'), 〜と言う ('dice che...'). La frase citata va in forma piana prima di と: あしたはあめだとおもう ('penso che domani piova'). と funziona come le virgolette del pensiero o del discorso. È lo strumento base per dire cosa pensi e per riportare le parole altrui.",
    "en": "To express opinions and quote: 〜と思う ('I think that...'), 〜と言う ('says that...'). The quoted clause goes in plain form before と: あしたはあめだとおもう ('I think it'll rain tomorrow'). と works like quotation marks for thought or speech. It's the basic tool for saying what you think and reporting others' words."
  },
  "grammarRefs": [
    "gr-to-omou-to-iu"
  ],
